Ben makes a good point - that using the trap response model will lead to bias if it's not the right model. One reason to like the detector-specific model (~bk) is that it leads to a much smaller difference in density estimate than the blanket trap response model (~b), while often having lower AIC and hence dealing to MSA (model-selection anxiety). It's instructive to compare the density estimates from your different models and focus on big effects.

