Yeah. Thanks. There are loose ends, and you've put your finger on one: I don't know if modelled differences in detection among replicates are a problem or not. You can have something intermediate between complete independence and complete dependence. My hunch is that any resulting bias in var(A-hat) will be tiny; even the weighting I suggest had little effect in the example I checked, because CV(a) was pretty near constant.

The code will be more stable if you can wait a day or so. It will be good to build some experience on which to build advice to users. I'll be in touch.
Murray

