That doesn't tell us where Trap_Type came from...

But I have added the necessary line (one line!) to the code and repackaged it as pre-release 1.3.3 that you can get from www.otago.ac.nz/density/zip/openCR_1.3.3.tar.gz <http://www.otago.ac.nz/density/zip/openCR_1.3.3.tar.gz> (no Windows binary yet, but it seems you can do without). Hope this solves your problem - good to get some long jobs running over Christmas?
Murray

library(openCR)  # >= 1.3.3

# fake a trap covariate
covariates(traps(captdata)) <- data.frame(Trap_type = sample.int(2,100, replace = TRUE))
# test
msk <- make.mask(traps(captdata))
fit <- openCR.fit(captdata, type='secrCL', model = lambda0 ~ Trap_type, mask = msk)
coef(fit)
predict(fit, newdata = data.frame(Trap_type=1:2))

